+# Inventory source-parser repair
+
+Outline before implementation: task-owned branch `codex/meri-inventory-parser-20261017`, local base `4359e05bd11b7756d4f1d42fcd2243b3e07f126b`, separate `meri-inventory-next` worktree above public PR125. Sparse patterns were configured before materialization; the initial checkout contains 663 files/about 12.1MB, without heavy evidence archives or dependency installation. The existing task dependency directory is borrowed through a junction only where canonical contract loading requires it. Existing checkouts, release candidates, historical evidence and processes remain untouched.
+
+Owned tooling is only `scripts/general-reads/sources.mjs`, `inventory.test.mjs`, a cohesive focused source-parser test if needed, this report and bounded new evidence. Do not change runtime, SDK, source adapters, catalog, accepted scope, ledger, generated metadata, locks or native code. Parent owns independent review and a separate tooling draft publication; no stage/commit/publish is allocated here.
+
+Diagnose `parseDispatchProfiles` against the actual canonical dispatch source. Its current regexp unnecessarily requires the undefined-profile branch to be a one-line return; the real branch now contains validation while the explicit seven-profile rejection guards remain. Read those literal guards without evaluating imported source, preserve source ownership/provenance, and refuse missing, malformed, duplicate, unknown or inconsistent declarations. Check the adjacent original-skill admission parser against actual skill-server source and packaged IDs under the same rules, without importing the SDK or constructing a server. Preserve canonical inventory validation: later source inconsistency or committed historical drift is evidence to report, not permission to bypass assertions, regenerate snapshots or change integration order.
+
+Capture the initial parser/module-load failure before repair. Verify the parser with actual source and meaningful adversarial input, then run the existing inventory tests and CLI read-only checks/help. Retain every failed outcome before any repair or reclassification. Finish with source hashes, exact commands/outcomes, bounded evidence and process cleanup. No live HTTP/provider/database/AWS or credentials are used.
+
+Expanded tooling outline, approved after the first dry diagnostic: additionally own `inventory.mjs`, `inventory.test.mjs` and the current generated `docs/coordination/proposals/general-reads/inventory.json`. The unchanged inventory now fails honestly because its original 13-group integration priority omits 25 groups with current declared adapters. Canonical adapter metadata contains 35 rows/63 distinct operations/62 selected capabilities, versus the historical generated 10/18/17. Keep the original priority and append deterministic actual declared groups rather than writing another registry. Validate adapter references, uniqueness, source declarations and complete canonical bindings; test missing/unknown/malformed/duplicate counterexamples. Normalize actual repository-relative manifest/prose paths to POSIX so Windows does not lose all 13 original-manifest matches. Preserve catalog and capability invariants (97 contracts, 139 capabilities, 96 selected, 43 deferred), actual two-skill MCP admission and live zero. Review a strict in-memory generated delta before writing only the current snapshot; historical ledgers/reports/fixtures remain unchanged. Independent expanded source/dry-delta review is required before acceptance/publication.
+
+The parent then allocated exactly five missing curated `adapters.json` rows for already-published PR125 handlers, plus an official current-exposure-only refresh of the two ledger outputs if necessary. These rows describe acquisition personnel (2), disclosures (3), Florida budget (1), public reports (3) and research portfolio (2). They reconcile existing source presence; they add no handler, operation, SDK registration, authority, installation or qualification. Current canonical metadata now contains 40 handler directories and 74 unique operation references: 72 selected source reads (69 complete and 3 partial), one selected product-state read, and one retained historical operation.
+
+## Implementation and source ownership
+
+`sources.mjs` now statically decodes the literal negative admission guards in their actual exported owners: `assertOperationArguments`, `prepareOperationContext`, and `createOriginalSkillServer`. Both dispatcher owners must contain the same seven-profile list exactly once; MCP admission remains its actual two original skills. The undefined-profile branch can grow without invalidating extraction. Comments, strings, templates and regexps do not establish guards; moved/nested/duplicate owners, conflicting lists, dynamic/escaped/sparse arrays, incorrect refusal calls, unsupported weakening conditions and unknown identities fail closed. Dispatcher/SDK source is never imported or evaluated by this decoder. The existing canonical contract resolver remains the contract owner.
+
+Manifest and prose paths are normalized from the host separator to POSIX before comparison and provenance recording. All 13 original manifests now match on Windows. Declared adapter files are read and hashed; literal operation IDs preserve the previous evidence rule, and newly accepted unquoted route keys must bind exactly `/api/clio/tools/<same-operation-id>`. Wrong routes and bare object keys do not count. The pure inventory builder rejects missing/unknown/malformed bindings, duplicate contracts or operation declarations, effectful adapter operations, invalid/duplicate source paths, missing source declarations, invalid partial subsets and omissions from the actual handler-directory inventory. Its original 13-family priority is unchanged; the remaining 30 actual bound groups follow deterministically, without a second group registry. Partial presence remains separate from complete coverage and live availability.
+
+The five added metadata rows retain source-specific boundaries: acquisition's trusted current actorRole/Core PII and audit ownership, native disclosure and public-report one-pass normalization, retained portfolio scope/GET visibility, and Florida's existing Core/Intel projection with observation labels. Public-report and portfolio IDs are derived by their handlers; their actual finite contract validators are included in declaration evidence. Existing curated rows, funding Core51c and semantic KB Core59 qualifier statements were not rewritten.
+
+## Dry delta and historical preservation
+
+`inventory-dry-complete-source.{txt,json}` records the full structured in-memory delta reviewed before either generator wrote current artifacts. Only current provenance, adapter-presence counts/authorization, corresponding route-status fields, family ordering and adapter-dependent skill reconciliation changed. There are 56 capability/operation rows with newly reflected existing adapter presence. `search_capiro_data.inputSchema` also catches up to the already-published raw `DataSearchRequest` pointer; no public contract was edited. The catalog identity, 97-contract mapping, 139/96/43 scope split, product/write routing, all pending/null descriptor qualifiers, actual MCP two-skill admission and live zero remain unchanged. Inventory presence changes from historical 10 adapters/18 operation references/17 selected to current 40/74/73; it does not claim those operations are qualified.
+
+`exposure-dry-initial.{txt,json}` uses the official `generateExposure()` without writing. Every current exposure count is equal to the preceding published ledger, including 69 complete, 3 partial, 10 absent, SDK 71 operations/41 families and live zero. Exactly eight rows gain one reviewed helper/validator path each: acquisition search/detail, Florida project, CBO/GAO/CRS, and portfolio detail/changes. All other 88 rows and all other fields compare equal. Provenance adds those four helper/validator files and updates only the curated metadata hash. Both official generators were then run after independent dry review. The rendered ledger Markdown remains byte-identical because its displayed counts/claims are unchanged.
+
+The parent separately allocated two narrow historical-test corrections. First, historical Git inventory objects and each historical ledger's inventory provenance remain pinned to `6f4a359d04ef8f364ba1f621ed977c4cace80d066494cde73d61c8286502854c`; the editable current inventory instead has its own exact regeneration/CLI check. CSV comparisons, all eight serialized historical ledger fields, 43 exclusions, old handoff, funding/KB reports and first four-read receipts remain unchanged. Second, the PR119 five-read projection stays exactly historical; its comparison with current source metadata admits only the eight literal path additions above, with all remaining row fields and counts deep-equal. A separate test checks the exact five new metadata rows. Historical ledgers/projections/reports/fixtures were not regenerated.
+
+## Retained verification evidence
+
+All records below are in `inventory-parser-20261017/`, with complete raw console `.txt` and exact executable/argv/start/end/exit `.json` metadata. Tests use the existing Node24 runtime, `--preserve-symlinks --max-old-space-size=256`, serial test execution, and borrowed existing root/conversation dependency junctions. No package installation, copied dependency tree, live request or broad product test/build was performed.
+
+- `inventory-module-initial`: exit 1 before any assertions, `INVENTORY_SOURCE: Gateway dispatch profile list not found`; `inventory-cli-initial`: exit 3 for that same source failure.
+- `parser-focused-initial`: 15/15 pass; owner-binding review then added moved/nested/duplicate-owner negatives, `parser-owner-review`: 17/17 pass. These are overlapping checkpoints, not additive counts.
+- `inventory-module-after-parser`: exit 1 on the real stale adapter-order consistency error; `inventory-cli-after-parser`: exit 3, with no write. `inventory-cli-help`: exit 0 and unchanged documented exit semantics.
+- `current-source-diagnostic`: exit 0, exposes the original 35 declared paths/63 references, 25 omitted groups and Windows 0/13 original-manifest matches.
+- `inventory-dry-initial`: exit 1 on actual handler coverage (40 current handler directories versus 35 declared); this was fixed only after exact five-row metadata allocation. `inventory-dry-complete-source`: exit 0 after approved metadata reconciliation. Both current snapshots remained untouched during dry review.
+- `inventory-pre-generation`: 32/34 pass; one expected current snapshot drift and one incorrect test spelling (`search_legal_news`, corrected to canonical `search_legiwatch_news`). Both failed outcomes are retained.
+- `inventory-generate-reviewed` and `exposure-refresh-reviewed`: official allocated writes both exit 0, producing exactly their reviewed dry hashes.
+- `tooling-integrated-initial`: parser/inventory 34 pass; exposure module fails before assertions because the root-only dependency junction does not contain the existing conversation SDK overlay. The failure was resolved by borrowing the already-present conversation dependency junction; `exposure-focused-overlay`: 37/37 pass, with no source/assertion weakening.
+- `tooling-integrated-final`: the then-current 71/71 pass, with inventory and exposure CLI checks both exit 0. This is an earlier checkpoint, superseded by independent review's valid regexp-only owner counterexample.
+- `parser-regexp-repro`: 19/20 pass; the valid regexp-only MCP owner falsely appeared to declare executable admission. The regression failure is retained. The decoder now refuses every ambiguous/unsupported slash position rather than tokenizing possible regexp contents as a guard. Statement/control/await/binary-expression decoys, alone or preceding a real guard, are covered.
+- `tooling-regexp-final` and `tooling-lexical-final`: both retain actual source-load failures after the conservative slash fix. The original template skipper split an existing nested portfolio path template; bounded opaque nested-template/interpolation handling fixes that boundary without exposing template contents. The actual wire codec also contains `Math.ceil(MAX_BYTES*4/3)`; only proven decimal-number operands are admitted as division. Variable operands, BigInt/scientific syntax and ambiguous trailing slash remain refused. Interpolation regexp/division/comment grammar is unsupported and fails closed. The limits are intentional static-decoder boundaries, not an attempt to parse/evaluate arbitrary JavaScript.
+- `tooling-numeric-final`: **74/74 pass**, exit 0, no failures/skips/cancellations, 4,704.1429ms. This final run contains 22 source/parser tests, 15 inventory tests and 37 current-exposure controls. Repeated checkpoints and reviewer runs are overlapping evidence, not additive tests.
+
+The initial sparse `add --no-cone --stdin` spelling was rejected by this Git version before changing checkout patterns. Repeating `add --stdin` under the already-configured non-cone mode succeeded; only needed source/fixture imports and small immutable comparison evidence were materialized. `sparse-import-closure.txt` records the exact additional static import files. No other checkout or dependency directory was changed.
+
+## Frozen result and limits
+
+The current inventory SHA-256 is `0616014eefedd534ffa7d6a9774a65873434bca13f54eb8a0d163397fca53cfd`; current ledger JSON is `0a97c45b959d8181290fea4fe1c87a89c00509c68da361ae013089dc737ab26b`. The ledger Markdown is unchanged at `5dddf86badb03152fdedeca8f0eb8dd4b658b5df0e421d1d4d6db13287435664`. `frozen-files-final.json` records exact source/test/current-artifact byte counts and SHA-256 values; the earlier `frozen-files.json` remains a pre-regexp-review checkpoint. Final standalone CLI records and whitespace check are preserved separately.
+
+All task-owned command/test sessions exited; no server, watcher or background process was started. The two local dependency junctions borrow existing directories for reproducible review and contain no new installed packages. This dedicated worktree remains unstaged/uncommitted for the parent to independently accept and publish as a separate tooling PR. Final expanded independent review is required before publication. No product code, SDK policy, Core code, public/private retrieval contract, lockfile, runtime startup, migration, infra, credentials or live access changed; this work supplies current offline inventory evidence only.
+
+Raw evidence uses the captured host bytes. Publication must preserve those bytes and verify staged blob hashes rather than silently normalizing diagnostic line endings. Historical evidence and the protected release/source checkouts remain untouched.
