+# Independent inventory tooling review
+
+Disposition: **ACCEPT_SOURCE** for the frozen tooling and reviewed current generated data. No blocking source findings remain. This review is against local base `4359e05bd11b7756d4f1d42fcd2243b3e07f126b`, tree `aa31607522e34df3bca96b9e381caae0d599d398` (published PR125 source), on the separate `codex/meri-inventory-parser-20261017` worktree. Final staged-tree and raw-evidence preservation acceptance is a separate identity check before publication.
+
+I read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/IMPLEMENTATION-STANDARDS.md`, the actual dispatch and skill-admission owners, all changed tooling/tests, the five reconciled adapter declarations and their existing handlers/validators, the generated dry delta, current ledger delta and retained failed/final receipts. I changed only this new review report; no staging, source repair, generator write, dependency installation or native access was performed by this reviewer.
+
+## Findings resolved
+
+The obsolete dispatch regexp depended on an unrelated one-line undefined-profile return. The replacement reads only literal negative rejection guards in the two distinct exported canonical owners, `assertOperationArguments` and `prepareOperationContext`; both must agree. The skill list comes from the actual `createOriginalSkillServer` rejection guard and remains exactly the two admitted original skills. Packaged manifests bound consistency without manufacturing admission. The decoder neither imports nor evaluates dispatcher/SDK source.
+
+Independent review first required owner binding: guards moved into duplicate, nested, non-exported or unrelated helpers cannot establish admission. A later valid regexp-only canonical-owner counterexample falsely established skill admission. That finding was reproduced and retained in [parser-regexp-repro.txt](inventory-parser-20261017/parser-regexp-repro.txt). The final decoder refuses ambiguous slash syntax, keeps bounded nested templates opaque, and permits only proven decimal-number division needed by the existing codec's `*4/3`. Regression cases cover the regex-only owner, control/await/binary decoys, decoy plus a real guard, nested templates and unsupported arithmetic/interpolation syntax. The actual current sources still parse. This is an intentionally bounded source decoder, not an arbitrary JavaScript parser.
+
+Operation declaration evidence preserves exact literal IDs. An unquoted key counts only when its value is the exact `/api/clio/tools/<same-id>` route; comments, prose, bare keys and wrong/different-operation routes do not establish that evidence. Canonical bindings, effectful/unknown/duplicate declarations, actual handler-directory coverage and partial subsets retain explicit rejection checks. Host-relative manifest/prose paths are normalized to POSIX. All 13 original manifests match on Windows.
+
+## Generated data and preserved scope
+
+The independently reproduced in-memory render matches the accepted dry SHA-256 `0616014eefedd534ffa7d6a9774a65873434bca13f54eb8a0d163397fca53cfd`. Only current provenance, adapter-dependent counts/authorization/route status/reconciliation and family ordering change, plus the already-published `search_capiro_data` raw input-schema pointer. The original 13-family priority remains, followed deterministically by the other 30 actual canonical groups.
+
+The five new metadata rows describe 11 already-published operations: acquisition personnel (2), disclosures (3), Florida budget (1), public reports (3) and research portfolio/detail changes (2). Their native fixed routes, existing source handlers, source-specific authority boundaries, current SDK policy and canonical constructors already exist. No operation or runtime registration is added by this tooling PR. In particular, research portfolio, portfolio changes and Florida budget project reads remain explicit.
+
+Current inventory presence is 40 handler directories, 74 operation references and 73 selected capabilities with an adapter. Its 72 selected source reads with an adapter comprise **69 complete plus 3 partial**; presence is not qualification. Current exposure remains **69 complete / 3 partial / 10 absent = 82**, 13 incomplete operations across 10 families, SDK **71 operations / 41 families**, live **0**. All 97 catalog descriptors retain unimplemented/pending/null-handler status. The catalog's 139 capabilities, 96 selected, 43 excluded, contract mapping, actual MCP admission and product/governed routes are unchanged.
+
